<h2>Palm Springs at a Glance</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Best for:</strong> Couples, architecture enthusiasts, desert scenery, relaxed weekends, memorable dining, and distinctive accommodations.</li>
<li><strong>Ideal trip:</strong> Two nights and approximately 48 hours.</li>
<li><strong>Where to stay:</strong> Downtown Palm Springs or the Historic Tennis Club neighborhood.</li>
<li><strong>Getting around:</strong> Downtown is walkable, but a car is helpful for architecture sightseeing, Indian Canyons, and the Aerial Tramway.</li>
<li><strong>Best time to visit:</strong> Late fall through early spring.</li>
<li><strong>Reservations:</strong> Book accommodations ahead, particularly during popular weekends. Check restaurant reservations and attraction schedules.</li>
<li><strong>Suggested pace:</strong> One or two major activities per day, with time left for spontaneous discoveries.</li>
</ul>
