<h2>Where to Stay in Palm Springs</h2>
<p>For a short getaway, where you stay can influence the entire experience.</p>
<p>Palm Springs is known for its distinctive accommodations, ranging from intimate midcentury boutique hotels to contemporary properties with rooftop pools and secluded desert retreats.</p>
<p>For a first visit, I would concentrate on three possibilities, each offering a different kind of weekend.</p>
<h3>Del Marcos Hotel — For Midcentury Character</h3>
<p>If part of your interest in Palm Springs is its architecture, Del Marcos Hotel offers an opportunity to experience that history firsthand.</p>
<p>Designed by architect William F. Cody, the hotel reflects the clean lines and relaxed indoor-outdoor living that helped define the city's architectural identity.</p>
<p>Its smaller scale and location near downtown make it an appealing choice for travelers who prefer a more intimate hotel experience.</p>
<p><strong>Best suited for:</strong> Couples and architecture enthusiasts who appreciate boutique accommodations with character.</p>
<p><a href="https://expedia.com/affiliates/palm-springs-hotels-del-marcos-hotel-adults-only.gHRUXBf" rel="sponsored noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Check availability at Del Marcos Hotel</a></p>
<h3>Kimpton Rowan Palm Springs — For Downtown Convenience</h3>
<p>For visitors who want restaurants, shops, and downtown attractions within easy reach, the Kimpton Rowan Palm Springs offers a different experience.</p>
<p>Its central location makes it convenient for exploring the city on foot, while its rooftop pool provides sweeping views of the surrounding mountains.</p>
<p>If you plan to spend much of your weekend enjoying downtown Palm Springs, this may be the most practical of our three recommendations.</p>
<p><strong>Best suited for:</strong> First-time visitors who value convenience, contemporary amenities, and easy access to downtown.</p>
<p><a href="https://expedia.com/affiliates/hotel-search-kimpton-rowan-palm-springs-hotel-by-ihg.2eVH3BF" rel="sponsored noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Explore rooms at Kimpton Rowan Palm Springs</a></p>
<h3>Korakia Pensione — For a Romantic Desert Retreat</h3>
<p>Korakia Pensione offers an atmosphere that feels removed from the ordinary.</p>
<p>With Moroccan- and Mediterranean-inspired architecture, intimate courtyards, and peaceful outdoor spaces, the property has a character quite different from the larger hotels and resorts.</p>
<p>It's the kind of place where spending an afternoon on the property can be as appealing as heading out to explore.</p>
<p><strong>Best suited for:</strong> Couples seeking a romantic, distinctive, and quieter desert getaway.</p>
<p><a href="https://expedia.com/affiliates/hotel-search-korakia-pensione.aJkMaeH" rel="sponsored noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">View accommodations at Korakia Pensione</a></p>
<p><strong>Our suggestion:</strong> Choose downtown convenience if sightseeing and dining are your priorities. Choose a distinctive boutique property if your accommodations are an important part of the experience.</p>
